<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c8714dfa6c5f2e8b76579edc634fa8fb3b3387c662e1d01aff3a7e7b50213761> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Credit line"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Harvard Art Museums/Arthur M. Sackler Museum, Gift of Richard R. Wagner" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/c956da87bc44a0ab30ff18ff14c4f2c217c3cd2efc899eb6b7adc205f5f96e1c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The fibula has an arching bow and a simple flattened catchplate folded into a U-shape. The bow is covered by a series of raised horizontal ridges. The spring is triple coiled. The pin is circular in section and flattened out to a square-section at the coil, becoming circular again at the juncture with the bow." .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1695c6881a5f8726ed34b6ada2fde4ff33caeed61c829d9843cb52ed9c22102> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Credit line"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Harvard Art Museums/Arthur M. Sackler Museum, Transfer from the Department of the Classics, Harvard University, Gift of Professor A. A. Howard" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d1ae266d4e1753b8f07527f916a12b99d678230fcfa871b9bdabe9f558814af7> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Credit line"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Harvard Art Museums/Arthur M. Sackler Museum, Gift of the Florence Gould Foundation, Dr. and Mrs. Jerome M. Eisenberg and William Collins Kohler, Purchase from the Alpheus Hyatt Purchasing Fund, Anonymous Fund in memory of Henry Berg, Henry George Berg Bequest, Gift in Gratitude to John Coolidge, Gift of Leslie Cheek, Jr., Director's Discretionary Fund" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d2ce4b18907e18c13bf03a0aa74370db3dc43419fcee2b6cc03e229545141d90> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Figure wears a high cylindrical Polos ( 3.1 cm) over long flowing hair. It has a triangular face, prominent nose, and was impressed from a worn mold. The head is hollow running from a hole in the top of the polos. The back of the body is oval, pressed by hand into the mold. Probably from a seated figure." .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/d8281702d49cd9d72b7f5977ca49614e288f621a1b6482e96e0d840da883be54> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Commentary"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "This vase is attributed to the Villa Giulia Painter, active in the mid-fifth century BCE. The painter favored scenes of everyday life and utilized stock figures to create harmonious compositions." .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/dc9378afdb69a540e8ce554dc9a1e7bc3f90421eb648744b2b64abc34f591adf> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Description"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Red-figure kalpis hydria. Rounded body with ogival foot, torus base and torus mouth. Relatively large side handles, tilting upwards. The scene depicts a nude youth in profile facing right with mantle draped over his left shoulder and forearm. He holds a staff in his left hand. Two women stand on either side. On the left, the woman runs to the left, her body frontal, and her head turned towards the youth. On the right, the woman stands frontal with her head to the left, facing the youth. Both women wear chitons and himations. 

Both women raise their left arms, bent at the elbows, in an apparent gesture of surprise or alarm, perhaps at the man's presence.  

Decoration is limited. The figures stand on a groundline consisting of a meander and are framed by a similar band. Preliminary drawings are visible and added red is used throughout for details. Vessel is unbroken with limited chipping.""" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/df4663bb363d76dade08777c9e7afa6d3dc80f054cd555c6bceada6b964e5745> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Credit line"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Harvard Art Museums/Arthur M. Sackler Museum, Transfer from the Department of the Classics, Harvard University, Gift of Dr. George H. Chase" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e083682bc28521395485359ad757cdb4cfa1c44d9ed2e83106006e58c5fec50c> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Credit line"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Harvard Art Museums/Arthur M. Sackler Museum, Transfer from the Department of the Classics, Harvard University" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e1a9c47e1c01c11c8f001271f3257750bda3491faafe3d0639d26fc2b698264e> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
    rdfs:label "Provenance"@en ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content """Pfeiffer-Hartwell Collection, Purchased in Athens.
Department of the Classics, Harvard University.
Transfer to Fogg Art Museum, 1977.""" .

<https://aa.perseus.org/id/text/e7f2546e086d501b58af2f000e46cfb27ab0c2c6bda6cb3701696fe15835761d> a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
